---An object that represents an initial VLAN subnet for the Amazon EVS environment. Amazon EVS creates initial VLAN subnets when you first create the environment. Amazon EVS creates the following 10 VLAN subnets: host management VLAN, vMotion VLAN, vSAN VLAN, VTEP VLAN, Edge VTEP VLAN, Management VM VLAN, HCX uplink VLAN, NSX uplink VLAN, expansion VLAN 1, expansion VLAN 2.
---@class aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo
---@field cidr aws.evs.Cidr The CIDR block that you provide to create an Amazon EVS VLAN subnet. Amazon EVS VLAN subnets have a minimum CIDR block size of /28 and a maximum size of /24. Amazon EVS VLAN subnet CIDR blocks must not overlap with other subnets in the VPC.

---The initial VLAN subnets for the environment. Amazon EVS VLAN subnets have a minimum CIDR block size of /28 and a maximum size of /24. Amazon EVS VLAN subnet CIDR blocks must not overlap with other subnets in the VPC.
---@class aws.evs.InitialVlans
---@field vmkManagement aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo The host VMkernel management VLAN subnet. This VLAN subnet carries traffic for managing ESX hosts and communicating with VMware vCenter Server.
---@field vmManagement aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo The VM management VLAN subnet. This VLAN subnet carries traffic for vSphere virtual machines.
---@field vMotion aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo The vMotion VLAN subnet. This VLAN subnet carries traffic for vSphere vMotion.
---@field vSan aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo The vSAN VLAN subnet. This VLAN subnet carries the communication between ESX hosts to implement a vSAN shared storage pool.
---@field vTep aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo The VTEP VLAN subnet. This VLAN subnet handles internal network traffic between virtual machines within a VCF instance.
---@field edgeVTep aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo The edge VTEP VLAN subnet. This VLAN subnet manages traffic flowing between the internal network and external networks, including internet access and other site connections.
---@field nsxUplink aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo The NSX uplink VLAN subnet. This VLAN subnet allows connectivity to the NSX overlay network.
---@field hcx aws.evs.InitialVlanInfo The HCX VLAN subnet. This VLAN subnet allows the HCX Interconnnect (IX) and HCX Network Extension (NE) to reach their peers and enable HCX Service Mesh creation.
